{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1527524-2-homebrew-orders","id":1527524,"title":"2 Homebrew Orders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-27T17:52:34-08:00","id":1527524,"title":"2 Homebrew Orders","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:26px\">The Seeker's of Night's Edge</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">On The Hunt For Magic</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A good Mage never stays idle, he seeks his Obsessions, he tries to find out secrets whenever they may hide he wants to know, to explore, to research. But a good researcher never stays idle, he goes into the field, knee deep into the mud looking for the magical gold. The Seeker's of Night's Edge are named for their common goal, to discover all the secrets of this world and a thousand others.<br /> <br /> Discovery is like a drug and they're quite addicted to it, they are not like the Mysterium who believe magic is dying all around them, on the contrary, they believe it simply needs to be perfected a bit and it will grow. that's why they go hunting for it when they feel it near.by<br /> <br /> They don't limit themselves to what comes from the Supernal either, anything magical is fair game.<br /> <br /> <b>Mages join The Seekers of Night's Edge</b> When they decide the other Orders can't teach enough , and their path must be walked as fast as possible. When they need to learn, when their Obsessions become all-consuming<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Core Beliefs: To take Power</span><br /> <br /> Magic has many uses, while the advancement of Gnosis is still the main goal of the Seekers, they still seek power for its many practical and esoteric uses, or simply because their Obsessions demand it. In a way, their main beliefs might make them seem simplistic, after all they simply hunt for knowledge to increase their Gnosis, there doesn't seem to be a higher calling about it. When this criticism is made,they simply counter it by saying that the knowledge, power and connections they made are anything but simple in any way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Use the Power</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Knowledge and magic are useless if locked in a vault or hoard, once the magic of the world has been liberated from its source and taken by the Seekers, it must be put to use, that can take many forms, for continuous use of Artifacts to the reading of grimoires to the exploration of Emanation Realms. All of it has a use, and all must be taken,for study if nothing else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Accord with Shadow</span><br /> <br /> The many shades of the supernatural in the Chronicles of Darkness held many secrets, more often than not it's unwise to simply steal what belongs to them under the cover of darkness, they are more accustomed to it anyway. Better to deal, hustle and batter for secrets with inhabitants of the other worlds for their secrets. Once those relationships and bonds are created though, they are hard to break and several network between this Order and the supernatural societies perdure to this day<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Perfect the World</span><br /> <br /> The Seekers have an interesting relationship with Perfected Materials, they fit well in Seeker philosophy. For when a material is elevated to a more supernal form, it becomes filled with secrets, something in the process of elevating a material to a higher status creates new lore to be discovered. Perfected jewels shine with Mysteries, Perfected Fire burns in a way that must be studied.<br /> <br /> They believe the whole world can be perfected the same way, through morality, spirituality a brand new state can be achieved by anything you can imagine. And this new stage brings in new secrets<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Caucus</span><br /> <br /> A Seeker Caucus is usually loud and chaotic with the sounds of debate and new discovery, and experiments either working or blowing up. New members are called simply Hunters, and teams of those Hunters are led into missions to recover powerful magic by Researchers. And when it's necessary to negotiate with supernatural creatures, they are led by Mediators<br /> <br /> The high ranking leaders of the Order are called Sages<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Mysteries</span><br /> <br /> <br /> You'd be hard pressed to find a Mystery the Seekers don't go after. They look through all of the Mysteries of the world with the eyes of those who already half own them. But they have a particular taste for the ones who change the nature of magic itself around them<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Magical Symbolism: Seekings</span><br /> <br /> <br /> The Seekers of Night's Edge want to know everything. And their magical Symbolism reflects their hunger for knowledge, the rush of taking something powerful and making it there's<br /> never quite fades away.<br /> The Seekers are the <i>Venatio Draconis</i>, The Hunt of the Dragon, representing that the heirs of Atlantis will never sit idle. Theirs is the will to change the World<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Hubris</span><br /> <br /> Some things are better left alone, and the Seekers all too often fail to see that. They have released their share of ancient things, Bound and curses in the world simply because they wanted to capture it for study.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:26px\">The Shining Ones</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Magic is Here</span><br /> <br /> <br /> The Shining Ones claim the supernal-fallen division is an inaccurate statement at best, they believe magic can be found everywhere, even the dullest rock can be polished until it shines. They build sanctums and demesnes and look for every way the Supernal touches the Fallen. They rarely try to lay claim to those places of power, rather they see themselves as gardeners that keep those places alive and growing, or jewelers who make sure their glow never fades. When enough places of power are created and rediscovered, when enough Artifacts shake the heavens. Then the Supernal\u2019s Truth will be plain to all to see.<br /> <br /> <b>Mages join The Shining Ones</b> when they want more people to see the wonder of the Supernal, they believe that everyone needs magic in their lives, they are community minded<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Core Beliefs: Ex Nihilo</span><br /> <br /> <br /> The Shining Ones believe all magic ultimately created itself, it's sentience or lack of it is and Whether there is moral character to magic itself is hotly debated. To a Shining One magic will simply appear somewhere,anywhere, if you give in enough time, but it's better for Mages to hurry it along. The most common name for this belief is \u201cEx nihilo\u201d. They also believe that Magic must be guided but not fully controlled, hence their reluctance to try and take control of any Supernal Mysteries they meet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Physicality and Metaphor are one</span><br /> <br /> Some say The Supernal World is made of Symbols and the Fallen World is seemingly made of pure physical matter, nothing could be farther from the Truth. A tree and the symbol of strength that describes it are One. Their separation is largely part of the Lie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Build Communities</span><br /> <br /> Going at it alone is a fool's game, a lone Mage has no hope of truly bringing glory to the world, much less to himself. That's perhaps the biggest stain among the Tyrannic Cults, they serve only themselves when they serve the Exarchs. Communities are the key to handle magic and bring it on the light<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Record the Knowledge</span><br /> <br /> <br /> The children are the future, and thus they need to be taught. Of all the Orders the Shining Ones makes the most use of Grimoires and Palimpsests. They know future generations will have their share of Awakened and they will need teaching,thus no knowledge will be withheld. Rotes and all other forms of knowledge are saved for the future<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Caucus</span><br /> <br /> The Shining Ones have very little in the way of hierarchy, but that doesn't mean they aren't organized. Instead of a tiered organization,they create specialized roles for each job that needs doing. Visionaries are for instance, the ones who study Aedes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Mysteries</span><br /> <br /> <br /> They look for Mysteries of Supernal origin more often than not. When something is not working the way it's supposed to, especially if that something is the laws of reality, it quickens their interest, they just might use it to bring their goals into fruition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Magical Symbolism: Epiphany</span><br /> <br /> The Shining Ones prever quick and sudden revelation than the slower and more ponderous kind. They are always looking for ways to induce it And use methods from entheogens to meditation and beyond to induce it.<br /> In Atlantean Symbolism they are <i>Gloria Draconis</i><br /> The glory if the dragon, bringing the majesty of the awakened city to all<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Hubris</span>:<br /> <br /> <br /> The Hubris of a Shining one manifests in a know it all attitude, they can often find themselves in a path where they simply won't accept their way is not the best way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-28-2023, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T07:14:39-08:00","id":1527548,"title":"","content":"The Seekers seem like they would have to manage a fine balancing act between the Ordo Dracul's experiments and the Hunters in Darkness' wish to protect loci. On one hand, the secrets of blood magic and the vampiric curse. But on the other, access to fetishes and the lost histories of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The Shining Ones seem to have a lighter approach to the Veil, what is their doctrine regarding incorporating magic into Sleeper's lives without triggering The Curse ? Their tenet of &quot;Physical form and metaphor are one&quot; seems very in line with Tamer Legacies, do they have any connection to them ?<br /> <br /> Lastly, I believe there is a typo in the Hubris section of the Shining Ones, I think you might have meant: they simply won't accept their way isn't the best way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T07:31:13-08:00","id":1527549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1527524-2-homebrew-orders?p=1527548#post1527548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seekers seem like they would have to manage a fine balancing act between the Ordo Dracul's experiments and the Hunters in Darkness' wish to protect loci. On one hand, the secrets of blood magic and the vampiric curse. But on the other, access to fetishes and the lost histories of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The Shining Ones seem to have a lighter approach to the Veil, what is their doctrine regarding incorporating magic into Sleeper's lives without triggering The Curse ? Their tenet of &quot;Physical form and metaphor are one&quot; seems very in line with Tamer Legacies, do they have any connection to them ?<br /> <br /> Lastly, I believe there is a typo in the Hubris section of the Shining Ones, I think you might have meant: they simply won't accept their way isn't the best way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi! Thanks for commenting!<br /> \u200b<br /> yeah, the Seekers' would indeed need to flex their negotiation muscles to be able to get secrets and lore from vampires and werewolves,especially the ordo dracul and hunters in darkness.<br /> THe Shining ones believe even the Heaviest Sleeper is still Sleeping lightly, and and are a hair's breath from Awakening, sometimes that's unrealistically optimistic. Sometimes it's True<br /> The Shining ones in some ways are the &quot;Tamers of Everything&quot;, and many Tamers belong to the Shining Ones, they often disagree on the controlling/taming part though<br /> I'll fix the typo, thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T15:38:38-08:00","id":1527667,"title":"","content":"The Seekers feel a bit disjointed; like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Discovery is like a drug and they're quite addicted to it </div> </div> </div>That's the tagline of the entire game. Every mage has that.<br /> <br /> [quote]...they are not like the Mysterium who believe magic is dying all around them,[quote]<br /> <br /> That's what the Guardians believe. Parts of the Mysterium used to believe that, but now it's more a heresy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...they believe it simply needs to be perfected a bit and it will grow. </div> </div> </div>That's actually what the Mysterium believe.<br /> <br /> Plus, the <i>Perfect the World</i> precept seems kinda unrelated to the hunter aesthetic. Partially the issue may be that we already have an order of hunters, the <i>Tremere</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, I like the Shining Ones. A nicer, less obviously megalomaniacal Ladder would really add an interesting contrast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T15:40:23-08:00","id":1527668,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Michael;n1527667]The Seekers feel a bit disjointed; like:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's the tagline of the entire game. Every mage has that.<br /> <br /> [quote]...they are not like the Mysterium who believe magic is dying all around them,<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> That's what the Guardians believe. Parts of the Mysterium used to believe that, but now it's more a heresy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's actually what the Mysterium believe.<br /> <br /> Plus, the <i>Perfect the World</i> precept seems kinda unrelated to the hunter aesthetic. Partially the issue may be that we already have an order of hunters, the <i>Tremere</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That being said, I like the Shining Ones. A nicer, less obviously megalomaniacal Ladder would really add an interesting contrast. </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your feedback. I'll think on it. I'll post some order merits soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}